  "title": "France’s Presidential Election: Teddy Riner’s Move Amid Political Extremes",
  "summary": "Five-times Olympic judo champion Teddy Riner, a proponent of unity, has announced plans to run for president of France, while the far-right leader Marine Le Pen is set to challenge the incumbent French president, Emmanuel Macron. The election highlights growing political polarization and the potential for a split between left and right.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Teddy Riner, a five-time Olympic gold medalist, announced his presidential campaign in the coming years.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The French president, Emmanuel Macron, is set to run for re-election after his 2025 re-election.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The election is expected to become a battleground between political extremes, with Riner aiming to “bring people together” and Le Pen seeking to unify the French political landscape.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
