  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "‘I know what it’s like to fight’- France’s most popular sportsman says he’s running for president",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/09/judo-star-teddy-riner-plan-france-presidential-election",
      "description": "<p>Five-times Olympic judo champion Teddy Riner says he is neither leftwing nor rightwing but would seek to ‘bring people together’</p><p>The French judo star and five-times Olympic gold medallist <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/article/2024/aug/02/teddy-riner-frances-favourite-son-adds-to-olympic-gold-tally\">Teddy Riner</a> has announced plans to run in next year’s presidential election, describing himself as someone neither leftwing nor rightwing but who would seek to “bring people together”.</p><p>With more than five months before the April-May ballot to replace Emmanuel Macron, the race has been shaping up to be a showdown between political extremes. Polls point to a hollowing out of the political centre, suggesting that the anti-immigrant National Rally leader Marine Le Pen could be the frontrunner, with the radical-left leader Jean-Luc Mélenchon trailing behind.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/09/judo-star-teddy-riner-plan-france-presidential-election\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-09T17:42:51"
    },
    {
      "title": "Judo star announces run for president of France",
      "link": "https://www.washingtonpost.com/world/2026/11/09/judo-star-announces-run-president-france/",
      "description": "“Fighting has always been a part of who I am,” five-time Olympic gold medalist Teddy Riner said. As president, he would try to compete in the 2028 Games.",
      "source_name": "Washington Post World",
      "published": "2026-11-09T21:14:42"
    }
